 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -18,8 +18,33 @@\n     Every row must give the same number of features. The classifier is linear in the\n     features (they are standardized and a bias is added), so nonlinear structure only\n     helps if a feature expresses it. Only the Python standard library may be used.\n-\n-    Current method: the raw inputs.\n     \"\"\"\n-    return list(row)\n+    x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6 = row\n+    \n+    # Safe log for skewed positive x3\n+    x3_log = math.log(x3 + 1) if x3 >= 0 else 0.0\n+    \n+    # Squared terms for nonlinearity\n+    x1_sq = x1 * x1\n+    x2_sq = x2 * x2\n+    x3_sq = x3 * x3\n+    x4_sq = x4 * x4\n+    x5_sq = x5 * x5\n+    x6_sq = x6 * x6\n+    \n+    # Key interactions for nonlinear boundaries\n+    x1_x2 = x1 * x2\n+    x1_x3 = x1 * x3\n+    x1_x4 = x1 * x4\n+    x1_x5 = x1 * x5\n+    x1_x6 = x1 * x6\n+    x2_x3 = x2 * x3\n+    x2_x4 = x2 * x4\n+    x2_x5 = x2 * x5\n+    x2_x6 = x2 * x6\n+    x3_x4 = x3 * x4\n+    x3_x5 = x3 * x5\n+    x4_x5 = x4 * x5\n+    \n+    return [x1, x2, x6, x3_log, x3_sq, x4, x5, x4_sq, x5_sq, x1_sq, x2_sq, x6_sq, x1_x2, x1_x3, x1_x4, x1_x5, x1_x6, x2_x3, x2_x4, x2_x5, x2_x6, x3_x4, x3_x5, x4_x5]\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
